{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will surely hide My face from them.</b> Not as they suppose when they say that I am not in their midst — for in truth, wherever they may be, My Shekhinah is present there, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Megillah 29a): בְּכָל מָקוֹם שֶׁגָּלוּ כוּ׳ — but I will hide My face from delivering them." "<b>For all the evil that he has done.</b> He himself." "<b>Because he has turned to other gods.</b> For in the troubles that befall them on account of their sin, they do not turn to Me for help, in repentance and prayer, but turn to escape through the intermediacy of those who serve other gods."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:49.141178066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}